2. Verify the API using curl

Run this command in PowerShell:

curl.exe -v --ssl-no-revoke -x http://127.0.0.1:8089 https://mlogin.sit.etrade.com/login/auth/v1_4

The --ssl-no-revoke option disables certificate revocation checking for this test while retaining other certificate validation.

If that still fails, test:

curl.exe -vk -x http://127.0.0.1:8089 https://mlogin.sit.etrade.com/login/auth/v1_4

The -k option disables certificate verification and should be used only for troubleshooting.

If you receive the JSON response containing:

{
  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "reason": "STEP_COMPLETED"
}

then the API is accessible through the proxy.

